;; The RTS's semantics of GHC's non-threaded runtime (HE4e; doc/haskell/HASKELL-EVAL-SURVEY.md, "As built: HE4d,
;; HE4e (write-ahead)"): throwTo blocking its thrower while the target masks (HES41 (a), rts/RaiseAsync.c's throwTo and
;; maybePerformBlockedException), the reachability GHC's collector decides (rts/sm/MarkWeak.c): blocked threads no root
;; reaches resurrected with BlockedIndefinitelyOnMVar, OnSTM or NonTermination (Schedule.c's resurrectThreads), weak
;; pointers whose keys no root reaches finalized (Weak.c's scheduleFinalizers: the C finalizers at once, the Haskell ones
;; by a thread running runFinalizerBatch), at performGC and when every thread is blocked; and the delimited
;; continuations of prompt# and control0# (rts/Continuation.c).



